cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Traj2: A Native Macro Library for Single and Multi-Outcome Group-Based Trajectory Modeling in SAS"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RU-AGING/AgingTrajectory_Library_NLMIXED-Model"
url: "https://ru-aging.github.io/AgingTrajectory_Library_NLMIXED-Model/"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.17605/OSF.IO/6FG5J
    description: Archival release on OSF
abstract: >-
  A SAS-native macro library for group-based trajectory modeling (GBTM),
  implemented entirely in PROC NLMIXED with no externally compiled code, so it
  runs in secure research environments such as the CMS Virtual Research Data
  Center where PROC TRAJ cannot be installed. The current release covers two
  outcome families: bounded ordinal scales via a class-specific cumulative
  probit with exp-incremented thresholds, and continuous measures with bounded
  support via a class-specific censored normal, including joint two-outcome
  trajectory estimation.
keywords:
  - group-based trajectory modeling
  - latent classes
  - longitudinal data
  - finite mixture model
  - ordinal probit
  - censored normal
  - joint trajectory
  - SAS
  - NLMIXED
